{"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"dynamicToolCall","id":"B2-model-010","namespace":null,"tool":"instruction_read","arguments":{"resource_id":"docs-public","spans":null},"status":"completed","contentItems":[{"type":"inputText","text":"<instruction>\n---\nname: sg-docs\ndescription: Maintain internal architecture, governance, context, metadata, and agent docs.\n---\n\n# sg-docs\n\n## Mission\n\n`sg-docs` is the public owner for internal architecture, governance, context, metadata, and agent documentation.\n\n## Scope Gate\n\nUse this for internal documentation. Resolve the product and internal documentation surface, load `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT/skills/references/intent-to-outcome-autonomy.md`, and keep public docs and audience content with `sg-content`.\n\n## Required References\n\nResolve `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT` through the shared canonical-path doctrine, verify the root and `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT/skills/300-sg-docs/SKILL.md` exist, then load that canonical engine for documentation governance and validation. If the root or file is missing, stop with a visible error; never fall back to a sibling runtime path. Treat `300-sg-docs` as expert/legacy only.\n\n## Validation\n\nUse the selected governance workflow's structure, metadata, and repository-consistency checks.\n\n## Stop Conditions\n\nStop and follow the runtime contract when the documentation boundary, ownership, source of truth, or required validation is unresolved.\n\n## Report Modes\n\nLoad `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT/skills/references/reporting-contract.md` before reporting; keep internal engine names out of user-facing reports.\n\n</instruction>"}],"success":true,"durationMs":174},"threadId":"01a11cef-d5b1-7841-8ded-fa68685c45c0","turnId":"01a11cef-dbad-7833-a94e-419a3dfd75bf","completedAtMs":1791486846295},"emittedAtMs":1791486846295}
